cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this skill, please cite it as below."
title: "fibre-tracking: per-fibre tracking and orientation measurement in X-ray CT of composites"
abstract: >-
  A Claude skill for tracking and measuring individual fibres in X-ray computed
  tomography or microscopy volumes of fibre-reinforced composites: per-fibre
  orientation, diameter, volume fraction, orientation tensor, and tracking across
  scans or resolutions. Includes a Laplacian-of-Gaussian cross-section detector, a
  ground-truth phantom generator and scoring tools for deciding whether a given
  scan can resolve fibres at all.
type: software
